{title: I Know Whom I Have Believed}
{artist: Daniel W. Whittle / James McGranahan}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response, Closing}
{key: D}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 4/4}
{score: i-know-whom-i-have-believed.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [D]know not why God's [G]wondrous [D]grace
To [A7]me He hath made [D]known
Nor [D]why, unworthy, [G]Christ in [D]love
Re[A7]deemed me for His [D]own
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
But "I [G]know whom I have be[D]lieved
And am per[Bm]suaded that He is [A7]able
To [D]keep that which I've com[G]mitted
Un[D]to Him a[A7]gainst that [D]day"
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [D]know not how this [G]saving [D]faith
To [A7]me He did im[D]part
Nor [D]how believing [G]in His [D]Word
[A7]Wrought peace within my [D]heart
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I [D]know not how the [G]Spirit [D]moves
Con[A7]vincing men of [D]sin
Re[D]vealing Jesus [G]through the [D]Word
Cre[A7]ating faith in [D]Him
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
I [D]know not what of [G]good or [D]ill
May [A7]be reserved for [D]me
Of [D]weary ways or [G]golden [D]days
Be[A7]fore His face I [D]see
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
I [D]know not when my [G]Lord may [D]come
At [A7]night or noon-day [D]fair
Nor [D]if I'll walk the [G]vale with [D]Him
Or [A7]"meet Him in the [D]air"
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
